{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;stream_event&quot;,&quot;event&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;content_block_delta&quot;,&quot;index&quot;:1,&quot;delta&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;input_json_delta&quot;,&quot;partial_json&quot;:&quot;&quot;}},&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;0b7f7c2b-8a4f-4fd3-9857-9d9fc16ceeaf&quot;,&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;a7bcf66a-5108-4fea-8248-deb28947f333&quot;}
{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;message&quot;:{&quot;role&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:[{&quot;tool_use_id&quot;:&quot;toolu_01DzLqBMEf6SQ8oqondtLxkf&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;tool_result&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;=== MyLatestStory.bml ===\n&lt;!--Workspace Playground — MyLatestStory\n  FQN: org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.MyLatestStory-->\n&lt;playground:MyLatestStory xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n  xmlns:type=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.type\&quot;\n  xmlns:playground=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground\&quot;>\n\n  &lt;baseType>\n    core:Documentation\n  &lt;/baseType>\n  &lt;is>\n    A random structured song produced by a workspace transform execution, in Spanish, about a futuristic city and a dog\n  &lt;/is>\n  &lt;documentation>\n    Produced by the \&quot;Create Poem\&quot; step of a BlockML workspace transform execution.\n    Each run discards whatever stood here before and writes a freshly composed\n    Spanish song about a futuristic city and a dog, carried as typed properties,\n    so none of the text below is stable or authoritative.\n  &lt;/documentation>\n  &lt;properties>\n    &lt;title type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>El can de la Avenida de Cristal&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/title>\n    &lt;artist type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>Los Faroles de Neón&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/artist>\n    &lt;song type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>(Estrofa 1)\nLa ciudad se levanta sobre rieles de vidrio,\nmil ventanas encendidas como ojos sin sueño,\ny en la plaza de acero, donde nadie pasea,\nun perro gris olfatea lo que el viento trajo.\n\n(Estrofa 2)\nNo lleva collar, ni número, ni dueño que lo llame,\nsolo el mapa de las calles guardado en su nariz;\nlos coches vuelan mudos, las farolas quieren hablar,\npero él persigue el eco de una vieja cicatriz.\n\n(Estribillo)\nCorre, can, corre, bajo el cielo de neón,\nque la Torre Nueve todavía tiene voz;\nsi el futuro es una máquina sin sitio para el corazón,\ntú serás el guardián de lo que fuimos los dos.\n\n(Estrofa 3)\nUn niño lo saluda desde un puente de titanio,\nle lanza un pan de luz que sabe a lluvia de verdad,\ny el perro mueve la cola como un péndulo de agua,\nmidiendo con su alegría la distancia a la ciudad.\n\n(Estribillo)\nCorre, can, corre, bajo el cielo de neón,\nque la Torre Nueve todavía tiene voz;\nsi el futuro es una máquina sin sitio para el corazón,\ntú serás el guardián de lo que fuimos los dos.\n\n(Puente)\nCuando se apaguen las pantallas y el ascensor se duerma,\ncuando el último dron regrese a su rincón,\nquedará su silueta recortada en el vapor,\nun latido analógico en mitad del procesador.\n\n(Final)\nLa ciudad se levanta sobre rieles de vidrio,\ny a sus pies late tibio un pequeño corazón;\nmañana habrá más torres, más silencio, más metal,\npero siempre habrá un perro cuidando la canción.&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/song>\n    &lt;language type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>Spanish&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/language>\n    &lt;date type=\&quot;type:DateTime\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>2026-09-07T22:20:46&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/date>\n  &lt;/properties>\n&lt;/playground:MyLatestStory>\n\n=== RandomBlock.bml ===\n&lt;!--Workspace Playground — RandomBlock\n  FQN: org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.RandomBlock-->\n&lt;playground:RandomBlock xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n  xmlns:type=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.type\&quot;\n  xmlns:playground=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground\&quot;>\n\n  &lt;baseType>\n    core:Documentation\n  &lt;/baseType>\n  &lt;is>\n    A midnight lending shelf of bicycle lamps outside an all-night bakery, where riders borrow a light and leave a coin or a warm roll in its place\n  &lt;/is>\n  &lt;documentation>\n    Produced by the \&quot;Create Random Block\&quot; step of playground:MyTestTransformation\n    during a BlockML workspace transform execution. Each run discards whatever\n    stood here before and writes freshly invented, arbitrary material, so none\n    of the names, numbers, or dates below are stable or authoritative.\n  &lt;/documentation>\n  &lt;properties>\n    &lt;title type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>The Lamp Shelf at Håkonsen's Night Bakery&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/title>\n    &lt;custodian type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>Minded by Trine Håkonsen, who bakes from two in the morning and clips fresh batteries into the lamps while the first loaves prove&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/custodian>\n    &lt;location type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>A weatherboarded bakery on Sildegata, one street back from the fish quay, where the harbour wind funnels between the ice plant and the chandlery&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/location>\n    &lt;summary type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>A pine shelf bolted beside the bakery door holds a row of red rear lamps and white front lamps, each on a short brass hook. The rule, chalked on a slate, is: take a lamp if yours has died, ride home safe, and bring it back within three nights or leave something for the tin — coins, a candle, or a roll still warm from your own kitchen. A ship's logbook on a chain records the lamp taken, the street it is headed for, and whether the borrower wants waking with a knock if it is not returned. Dock workers, nurses on the late shift, and one accordion teacher keep the shelf turning over; twice a winter the whole row goes out at once and Trine rides the streets at dawn collecting them back.&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/summary>\n    &lt;lampsOnTheShelfTonight type=\&quot;type:Integer\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>18&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/lampsOnTheShelfTonight>\n    &lt;loansLoggedThisMonth type=\&quot;type:Integer\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>204&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/loansLoggedThisMonth>\n    &lt;coinsInTheTin type=\&quot;type:Integer\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>1375&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/coinsInTheTin>\n    &lt;shelfLengthCentimetres type=\&quot;type:Integer\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>142&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/shelfLengthCentimetres>\n    &lt;recordedAt type=\&quot;type:DateTime\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>2026-09-07T22:16:33&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/recordedAt>\n    &lt;shelfMountedOn type=\&quot;type:DateTime\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>2021-02-17T04:05:00&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/shelfMountedOn>\n  &lt;/properties>\n&lt;/playground:RandomBlock>&quot;,&quot;is_error&quot;:false}]},&quot;parent_tool_use_id&quot;:null,&quot;session_id&quot;:&quot;0b7f7c2b-8a4f-4fd3-9857-9d9fc16ceeaf&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;78a8d541-51ce-4bf1-a7c9-9256558edeb4&quot;,&quot;timestamp&quot;:&quot;2026-09-07T20:32:22.832Z&quot;,&quot;tool_use_result&quot;:{&quot;stdout&quot;:&quot;=== MyLatestStory.bml ===\n&lt;!--Workspace Playground — MyLatestStory\n  FQN: org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.MyLatestStory-->\n&lt;playground:MyLatestStory xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n  xmlns:type=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.type\&quot;\n  xmlns:playground=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground\&quot;>\n\n  &lt;baseType>\n    core:Documentation\n  &lt;/baseType>\n  &lt;is>\n    A random structured song produced by a workspace transform execution, in Spanish, about a futuristic city and a dog\n  &lt;/is>\n  &lt;documentation>\n    Produced by the \&quot;Create Poem\&quot; step of a BlockML workspace transform execution.\n    Each run discards whatever stood here before and writes a freshly composed\n    Spanish song about a futuristic city and a dog, carried as typed properties,\n    so none of the text below is stable or authoritative.\n  &lt;/documentation>\n  &lt;properties>\n    &lt;title type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>El can de la Avenida de Cristal&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/title>\n    &lt;artist type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>Los Faroles de Neón&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/artist>\n    &lt;song type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>(Estrofa 1)\nLa ciudad se levanta sobre rieles de vidrio,\nmil ventanas encendidas como ojos sin sueño,\ny en la plaza de acero, donde nadie pasea,\nun perro gris olfatea lo que el viento trajo.\n\n(Estrofa 2)\nNo lleva collar, ni número, ni dueño que lo llame,\nsolo el mapa de las calles guardado en su nariz;\nlos coches vuelan mudos, las farolas quieren hablar,\npero él persigue el eco de una vieja cicatriz.\n\n(Estribillo)\nCorre, can, corre, bajo el cielo de neón,\nque la Torre Nueve todavía tiene voz;\nsi el futuro es una máquina sin sitio para el corazón,\ntú serás el guardián de lo que fuimos los dos.\n\n(Estrofa 3)\nUn niño lo saluda desde un puente de titanio,\nle lanza un pan de luz que sabe a lluvia de verdad,\ny el perro mueve la cola como un péndulo de agua,\nmidiendo con su alegría la distancia a la ciudad.\n\n(Estribillo)\nCorre, can, corre, bajo el cielo de neón,\nque la Torre Nueve todavía tiene voz;\nsi el futuro es una máquina sin sitio para el corazón,\ntú serás el guardián de lo que fuimos los dos.\n\n(Puente)\nCuando se apaguen las pantallas y el ascensor se duerma,\ncuando el último dron regrese a su rincón,\nquedará su silueta recortada en el vapor,\nun latido analógico en mitad del procesador.\n\n(Final)\nLa ciudad se levanta sobre rieles de vidrio,\ny a sus pies late tibio un pequeño corazón;\nmañana habrá más torres, más silencio, más metal,\npero siempre habrá un perro cuidando la canción.&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/song>\n    &lt;language type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>Spanish&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/language>\n    &lt;date type=\&quot;type:DateTime\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>2026-09-07T22:20:46&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/date>\n  &lt;/properties>\n&lt;/playground:MyLatestStory>\n\n=== RandomBlock.bml ===\n&lt;!--Workspace Playground — RandomBlock\n  FQN: org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.RandomBlock-->\n&lt;playground:RandomBlock xmlns=\&quot;http://blockml.org/bml\&quot;\n  xmlns:core=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.core\&quot;\n  xmlns:type=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.type\&quot;\n  xmlns:playground=\&quot;org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground\&quot;>\n\n  &lt;baseType>\n    core:Documentation\n  &lt;/baseType>\n  &lt;is>\n    A midnight lending shelf of bicycle lamps outside an all-night bakery, where riders borrow a light and leave a coin or a warm roll in its place\n  &lt;/is>\n  &lt;documentation>\n    Produced by the \&quot;Create Random Block\&quot; step of playground:MyTestTransformation\n    during a BlockML workspace transform execution. Each run discards whatever\n    stood here before and writes freshly invented, arbitrary material, so none\n    of the names, numbers, or dates below are stable or authoritative.\n  &lt;/documentation>\n  &lt;properties>\n    &lt;title type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>The Lamp Shelf at Håkonsen's Night Bakery&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/title>\n    &lt;custodian type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>Minded by Trine Håkonsen, who bakes from two in the morning and clips fresh batteries into the lamps while the first loaves prove&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/custodian>\n    &lt;location type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>A weatherboarded bakery on Sildegata, one street back from the fish quay, where the harbour wind funnels between the ice plant and the chandlery&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/location>\n    &lt;summary type=\&quot;type:Text\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>A pine shelf bolted beside the bakery door holds a row of red rear lamps and white front lamps, each on a short brass hook. The rule, chalked on a slate, is: take a lamp if yours has died, ride home safe, and bring it back within three nights or leave something for the tin — coins, a candle, or a roll still warm from your own kitchen. A ship's logbook on a chain records the lamp taken, the street it is headed for, and whether the borrower wants waking with a knock if it is not returned. Dock workers, nurses on the late shift, and one accordion teacher keep the shelf turning over; twice a winter the whole row goes out at once and Trine rides the streets at dawn collecting them back.&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/summary>\n    &lt;lampsOnTheShelfTonight type=\&quot;type:Integer\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>18&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/lampsOnTheShelfTonight>\n    &lt;loansLoggedThisMonth type=\&quot;type:Integer\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>204&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/loansLoggedThisMonth>\n    &lt;coinsInTheTin type=\&quot;type:Integer\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>1375&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/coinsInTheTin>\n    &lt;shelfLengthCentimetres type=\&quot;type:Integer\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>142&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/shelfLengthCentimetres>\n    &lt;recordedAt type=\&quot;type:DateTime\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>2026-09-07T22:16:33&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/recordedAt>\n    &lt;shelfMountedOn type=\&quot;type:DateTime\&quot;>\n      &lt;value>2021-02-17T04:05:00&lt;/value>\n    &lt;/shelfMountedOn>\n  &lt;/properties>\n&lt;/playground:RandomBlock>&quot;,&quot;stderr&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;interrupted&quot;:false,&quot;isImage&quot;:false,&quot;noOutputExpected&quot;:false}}
